      "content": "{\"ok\": true, \"count\": 77, \"items_by_type\": {\"table\": [{\"id\": \"SPACE_UNIT\", \"desc\": \"Space unit dimension table: one row per space unit (an organizational space-assignment unit such as a department, program, or office that receives space allocation), with space unit key/code, space unit name, the facilities organization it belongs to, and DLC key. Bridges FCLT_ORGANIZATION (organization attribution) and SPACE_DETAIL (rooms assigned to the space unit); used to group room counts and space statistics by space unit.\"}, {\"id\": \"SPACE_DETAIL\", \"desc\": \"Space assignment detail fact table: one row per physical room assigned to a space unit, with building/floor/space-unit/space-usage keys, room identifiers (building-room number and name, room number), room square footage, room counter, and building component. Used to count rooms per space unit or per building, and to analyze room size and usage distribution. Joins to SPACE_UNIT via SPACE_UNIT_KEY, FCLT_BUILDING via BUILDING_KEY, SPACE_FLOOR via FLOOR_KEY, and SPACE_USAGE via SPACE_USAGE_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"ZPM_ROOMS_LOAD\", \"desc\": \"Space-planning room load table: one row per room record from the space planning feed, with the building-room identifier, building component, floor (numeric or label such as 'G9'), space usage text (e.g. 'DSGN STUDIO', 'CONF RM'), space unit code, HR organization unit id, and room access level. Links rooms to SPACE_UNIT via SPACE_UNIT_CODE and to FCLT_ORGANIZATION/HR_ORG_UNIT via HR_ORG_UNIT_ID; used for floor/access-level/space-usage room analysis from the space-planning perspective, without the area and use-key columns carried by FCLT_ROOMS.\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_ORGANIZATION\", \"desc\": \"Facilities organization dimension table: one row per organization in the institute's hierarchical organization tree (levels 1-6, from institute-wide down to sub-units), with organization identifiers and names, parent and major-organization attribution, hierarchy level, assignable-space flag, course number for academic departments, description, DLC (department/lab/center) key and name, and cross-references to HR organization units. Parent of SPACE_UNIT (space assigned to organizations) and referenced by FCLT_ROOMS via FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY for room occupancy attribution.\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_ROOMS\", \"desc\": \"Facilities room inventory table: one row per physical room with building/floor keys, room identifiers, use classifications (major/minor use), organization assignment, area in square meters, access level, and geographic coordinates. Joins to FCLT_BUILDING via FCLT_BUILDING_KEY; referenced by COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.MEET_PLACE via FCLT_ROOM_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"FAC_ROOMS\", \"desc\": \"Facilities room snapshot table with the same room inventory structure as FCLT_ROOMS (building/floor keys, room identifiers, major/minor use classifications, organization assignment, area, access level, coordinates) but keyed by FAC_ROOM_KEY and joining the FAC_* family (FAC_BUILDING, FAC_FLOOR, FAC_ORGANIZATION). Used as an alternative room source when FAC_* family keys are involved.\"}, {\"id\": \"SPACE_SUPERVISOR_USAGE\", \"desc\": \"Space supervisor usage fact table: one row per supervisor (MIT_ID) recording how much space they supervise and for how many departments: department count, department DLC key list (comma-separated when multiple), number of supervisees, supervised square footage, research volume, and derived ratio measures (sqft per supervisee, sqft per research volume, research volume per sqft). Joins to SPACE_UNIT and other DLC-carrying tables via DEPT_NAMES = DLC_KEY (only single-department rows match); used for supervisor space-usage and research-volume statistics per department/DLC.\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_ROOMS_HIST\", \"desc\": \"Historical facilities room table: one row per room per fiscal period (FISCAL_PERIOD in YYYYMM format; current data covers period 201505), preserving each room's identifiers, floor, use classifications, organization assignment, area, access level, and coordinates over time. Fiscal-period counterpart of FCLT_ROOMS; joins to current room records via FCLT_ROOM_KEY and to buildings via FCLT_BUILDING_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY\", \"desc\": \"Bridge table mapping facilities organizations to their department/lab/center (DLC) keys: one row per organization-DLC key assignment. Used to filter organizations that have a non-null DLC key assignment before joining FCLT_ORGANIZATION (via FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY or DLC_KEY) for DLC-level facility and room statistics.\"}, {\"id\": \"SPACE_USAGE\", \"desc\": \"Space usage classification lookup table: one row per space usage key with its usage name (e.g. classroom, office, lab usage categories). Referenced by SPACE_DETAIL via SPACE_USAGE_KEY to decode the usage classification of assigned rooms.\"}, {\"id\": \"SPACE_FLOOR\", \"desc\": \"Space-domain floor lookup table: one row per floor key with the floor number/label and floor name. Referenced by SPACE_DETAIL via FLOOR_KEY to attach floor identity to assigned rooms; a lightweight floor reference without the area measures carried by FCLT_FLOOR or FAC_FLOOR.\"}, {\"id\": \"FAC_BUILDING\", \"desc\": \"Facilities building snapshot table (FAC_* family): one row per physical building with the same building attribute structure as FCLT_BUILDING (number/name, type, ownership, use, occupancy class, gross/assignable/non-assignable areas, number of rooms, key dates, site, coordinates) but keyed by FAC_BUILDING_KEY and joining the FAC_* family (FAC_ROOMS, FAC_FLOOR, FAC_BUILDING_ADDRESS, FAC_ORGANIZATION). Used as the building dimension when FAC_* family keys are involved; FCLT_BUILDING is the counterpart in the FCLT_* family.\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_BUILDING\", \"desc\": \"Facilities building inventory table: one row per physical building with building number/name, type (e.g. ACADEMIC), ownership, use, occupancy class, gross/assignable/non-assignable areas, number of rooms, key dates (built/acquired/occupied), site and geographic coordinates. Parent of FCLT_ROOMS via FCLT_BUILDING_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"HR_ORG_UNIT\", \"desc\": \"HR organization unit dimension table: one row per HR organization unit with unit key/ID/title, unit level classification (ALL MIT, TOP LEVEL, DEPARTMENTS, SUB DEPARTMENT, ORGANIZATION LEVEL, NON HIERARCHY ORG UNITS), HR department identifiers and name variants (short, long, alphabetical), organization hierarchy area names (school area, top level, root), the full HR hierarchy path levels 1-7 (each with ID, sort order, and name), and DLC_KEY/DLC_NAME cross-references to departments/labs/centers. Joined from FCLT_ORGANIZATION and MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY via DLC_KEY to attach HR department attributes (title, level, department name, long name, hierarchy path) to facilities organizations and DLCs; a single DLC_KEY can map to multiple HR org unit rows, so joins via DLC_KEY may fan out.\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_MAJOR_USE\", \"desc\": \"Facilities major use classification lookup table (FCLT family): one row per major use code (e.g. CLASSRMS classrooms, OFFICES offices, LABS laboratories, RESIDENT residential) with its short code, description, and assignable-space flag. Joined from FCLT_ROOMS via FCLT_MAJOR_USE_KEY to decode a room's major use; current snapshot only, use FCLT_MAJOR_USE_HIST for fiscal-period historical variants.\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_FLOOR\", \"desc\": \"Facilities floor inventory table: one row per floor of a building (floor key formatted '<building key>-<floor>'), with floor number/label, gross, assignable and non-assignable areas of the floor, sort sequence, level identifier, building wing, and access level. Child of FCLT_BUILDING via FCLT_BUILDING_KEY and parent of FCLT_ROOMS via FCLT_FLOOR_KEY; used for per-floor area aggregation and floor-level filtering (e.g. floors with assignable area above a threshold).\"}, {\"id\": \"FAC_ORGANIZATION\", \"desc\": \"Facilities organization snapshot table with the same hierarchical organization structure as FCLT_ORGANIZATION (organization identifiers, parent/major organization, level, assignable flag, course number, description, HR cross-references) but keyed by ORGANIZATION_KEY and carrying D_CODE instead of DLC_KEY/DLC_NAME. Contains fewer organizations than FCLT_ORGANIZATION; used as an alternative organization dimension in FAC_* family queries.\"}, {\"id\": \"MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY\", \"desc\": \"Master department hierarchy table: one row per department/lab/center (DLC) under the 'Standard Hierarchy' hierarchy type, recording the DLC key/code/name and its five-level hierarchy path from the institute root (level 1 'All Departments') through executive areas down to the DLC's placement, with each level's code and name (null for levels deeper than the DLC's position). Joins to HR_ORG_UNIT and FCLT_ORGANIZATION via DLC_KEY; used to report or filter the master-hierarchy placement (school/area path) of a DLC, and as a DLC scope filter when only DLCs present in the standard hierarchy should be included.\"}, {\"id\": \"HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW\", \"desc\": \"Newer HR organization unit dimension table: one row per HR organization unit with the same unit/department identity and hierarchy-path structure as HR_ORG_UNIT (unit key/ID/title/level, HR department code and name variants, school-area/top-level/root names, hierarchy path levels 1-5, DLC_KEY) but a shallower hierarchy path (levels 6-7 absent), no HR_DEPARTMENT_ID and no DLC_NAME column, and an extra HR_DEPARTMENT_ABBR abbreviation column. Holds more unit rows than HR_ORG_UNIT (691 vs 641, including units absent from HR_ORG_UNIT); use HR_ORG_UNIT when DLC_NAME or the deeper hierarchy path is required, HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW for the newer unit coverage.\"}, {\"id\": \"FAC_FLOOR\", \"desc\": \"Facilities floor snapshot table (FAC_* family): one row per floor of a building with floor number/label, gross, assignable and non-assignable areas, sort sequence, level, wing, and access level. Same floor structure as FCLT_FLOOR but keyed by FLOOR_KEY/BUILDING_KEY joining FAC_ROOMS.FLOOR_KEY and FAC_BUILDING.FAC_BUILDING_KEY; used as the floor source when FAC_* family keys are involved.\"}], \"metric\": [{\"id\": \"dw_3410\", \"desc\": \"For rooms with an area greater than 300 and located in buildings with more than 100 rooms, show the building's long name, the room's full name, the room's area, and the row number within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by the building's long name, along with the name of the space unit, the associated organization name, and both the variance and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the organization numbers for all organizations linked to that space unit (considering only space units with a non-null DLC key and organizations with assignable status), where the room and the space unit share the same organization key. List the columns in the following order: building's long name, room's full name, room's area, window row number, space unit name, organization name, organization number variance, and organization number standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1465\", \"desc\": \"For each department in the Provost Area at the School of Science level, excluding the Biology department, and for each organization within those departments (excluding organizations with IDs '138' and '250'), show the department name, department code, organization name, organization ID, the maximum average organization number within each department code group, and the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the area of rooms assigned to the organization (considering only organizations with more than 5 rooms and excluding organizations named 'ADMISSIONS'), ordered by department name and organization name. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1833\", \"desc\": \"For each department and subject grade type where the subject is offered in the current academic year, is letter graded, and the department is Mathematics (Course 18), provide the number of subjects, the minimum total units, the school name, the department phone number, the organization name, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the areas of its rooms, and the department's DLC name, including subtotals for each department (the corresponding department field is 'SUBTOTAL') and a grand total across all departments (the corresponding department field is 'TOTAL'). Do not repeat the department if it is the same as the previous row. Only include organizations that have more than 5 rooms, are associated with a non-null DLC key, and are not the 'ADMISSIONS' department or the 'Political Science' department. Sort the table by department, grade type, and descending standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of room areas. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4025\", \"desc\": \"For rooms with a square footage of 150, show the space unit code, space unit name, and the maximum rank within each space unit code group, and for each of those space units, show the major organization, top-level HR organization name, HR department name, the average, variance, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the organization numbers for each HR department name, considering only organizations that are assignable and have a non-null organization number. The results should include the space unit code, space unit name, maximum rank, major organization, top-level HR organization name, HR department name, average organization number, organization number variance, and organization number standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP), in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3235\", \"desc\": \"For each department name and its corresponding facility organization key where the department is in the Provost Area, provide the number of organizations, the minimum department hierarchy level 3 code, the range, variance, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the number of HR organization units per facility organization (considering only those with a non-null DLC key and where the hierarchy type is 'Standard Hierarchy'), listing the results in order by department name and facility organization key. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1190\", \"desc\": \"For each building where the building type is 'ACADEMIC', the building is not the Brown Building, and the building has more than 3 historical records, give the building name, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the assignable area across its historical records, the average area of its rooms, and the variance of the area of its rooms, including only buildings that are academic buildings or have building number '32'. List the results in descending order of the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the assignable area. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4590\", \"desc\": \"For organizations with an organization level of 5, show the organization name, organization ID, DLC name, HR org unit title, HR department name, HR org unit level, and assign row numbers within each HR department name group ordered by organization name. For each such organization, for each room with area greater than 200 and assignable major use, show the building room, floor, room number, space ID, area, major use name, major use description, and the minimum area value over each major use group. Additionally, for each such room, show the HR org unit title and HR org unit level from the HR_ORG_UNIT table (joined via DLC_KEY), and the difference between the room's area and the minimum area for its major use. Order the results by HR department name, organization name, and major use. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3890\", \"desc\": \"For each major use description, list the building-room identifier, area, major use description, and assign row numbers within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by the major use description, as well as the organization name, department name, department code, department long name, department level, and the average organization number in a window of 2 preceding and 2 following rows grouped by the organization parent, ordered by the organization name, but only include those organizations whose organization number is greater than the average organization number of their parent group. For each major use description, include a grand total row for all rooms in the format of (null, null, major use description, total rooms) and only include rooms whose organization matches the filtered organizations. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_385\", \"desc\": \"For rooms in the Stata building (building 32) in buildings with an access level of 2, show the room key, building key, floor, major use description, area, and the average area over a window of 2 preceding and 2 following rows grouped by the floor's sort sequence and ordered by the room's area, but only include rooms whose area is greater than the average area for their floor. Exclude rooms whose major use description includes 'STORAGE'. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4271\", \"desc\": \"For rooms on floor 2 with access level 1, show the space unit, the maximum row number (within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by building room) for each space unit, the building room, the organization name, the department name, and the difference between the access level of the room and the average access level for that department. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_505\", \"desc\": \"For each building, what is the building name, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the assignable area across its historical records, and the average non-assignable area across its historical records, considering only buildings with more than 3 historical records, with a nonzero assignable area, and that are academic buildings? Additionally, restrict the results to buildings at MIT. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1888\", \"desc\": \"For each academic building in Cambridge, MA (excluding the Stata building), with more than 1 room and a non-null building name, and that is also an academic building at MIT with more than 10 rooms, show the building key, building name, building type, the number of historical records, the total assignable area across all historical records, the average number of rooms per historical record, the range, variance, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the areas of its rooms, and the total assignable area of the building at MIT, considering only buildings that satisfy all these criteria. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4562\", \"desc\": \"For each organization with an organization level of 5 whose space unit is among the top 10 space units by number of rooms, display the organization name, organization key, description, space unit, space unit key, the average organization key within each organization key group ordered by space unit key, the count of rooms for each space unit, and the building with the highest number of rooms in that space unit, along with the count of rooms in that building. Order the results by the count of rooms descending and then by space unit key. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4627\", \"desc\": \"For organizations with an organization level of 5, show the organization name, organization ID, DLC name, HR org unit title, HR department name, HR org unit level, and assign row numbers within each HR department name group ordered by organization name. For each such organization, for each room with area greater than 200 and assignable major use that belongs to the organization, show the building room, floor, room number, space ID, area, major use name, major use description, and the minimum area value over each major use group. Additionally, for each such room, show the HR org unit title and HR org unit level from the HR_ORG_UNIT table (joined via DLC_KEY). Present the results with the columns: organization name, organization ID, DLC name, HR org unit title, HR department name, HR org unit level, row number, building room, floor, room number, space ID, area, major use name, major use description, minimum area per major use, HR org unit title (from HR_ORG_UNIT), and HR org unit level (from HR_ORG_UNIT), in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_488\", \"desc\": \"Among all academic buildings at MIT, which building use type has the largest variance in room area, and what is the name of the building with the largest total room area for that use type? Show the building use, the area variance, and the building name with the largest total room area for that use type. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4061\", \"desc\": \"For each department and academic year, show the department name, academic year, academic year description, and the geometric mean of the total units for all subjects offered by the department in regular terms with total units greater than zero, along with, for each academic building where these subjects are held and which has rooms larger than 40 square meters, the building name, the average, range, and variance of the room areas, as well as the total assignable area of the building and the year the building was built. The results are ordered by department name, academic year (descending), and room area range (descending). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2528\", \"desc\": \"For each floor in the Stata building (building 32), what is the largest room square footage and the name of the building room with that largest square footage for rooms loaded into the warehouse on 19-DEC-24 with a largest room square footage greater than 100, and for each space unit on that floor with a room square footage greater than 10, what are the building room name, room number, room square footage, the average room square footage within the floor, and the floor's warehouse load date? List the results showing floor name, largest room name, largest room square footage, building room name, room number, room square footage, average room square footage per floor, and floor warehouse load date, ordered by floor name and room square footage. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4773\", \"desc\": \"For each organization with an organization level of 5 and for rooms on floor 2 that are associated via space unit code, show the organization name, organization key, description, space unit, space unit key, the average organization key within each organization key group ordered by space unit key, the building room, space usage, the HR org unit title, the department name, the minimum access level in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the building component, and the HR org unit level and department code for each room, ordered by organization name and building room. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4776\", \"desc\": \"For rooms with an area greater than 300 that are associated with departments in the \\\"Provost Area\\\", show the building-room identifier, floor number, major use description, organization name, DLC key, the average area in a window of 2 preceding and 2 following rows grouped by department code and ordered by area, the department code, department name, school area name, and the rank of each department within its school area based on department code. Additionally, include the department's full name from the HR organization unit and the department's hierarchy level 3 name from the master department hierarchy. Present the results ordered by building-room identifier and department code. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1488\", \"desc\": \"For each academic building at MIT and each of its floors with total assignable area greater than 5000 and at least one room with access level 1 or 2, provide the building's long name, the floor number, the range and variance of the area of rooms on that floor (considering only rooms with access level 1 or 2), the range and variance of the assignable area of its floors that have at least one room, and the total number of rooms in the building. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}], \"concept\": [{\"id\": \"concept_room_space_inventory\", \"desc\": \"Tables recording the physical room inventory and its space assignment: SPACE_DETAIL (rooms assigned to space units with usage classification and square footage), FCLT_ROOMS (facilities room inventory with use classifications, organization assignment, and area in square meters), FAC_ROOMS (the FAC_* family room snapshot with the same structure as FCLT_ROOMS but FAC_* keys), and ZPM_ROOMS_LOAD (space-planning room load feed with floor, space usage text, access level, and space unit code / HR org unit id links). They jointly answer questions about how many rooms exist, room sizes, room usage, and which organization/space unit occupies rooms, but differ in assignment perspective, key family, and area units.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_space_unit_dimension\", \"desc\": \"Space unit lookup tables identifying the organizational units that receive space allocation: SPACE_UNIT (with FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY organization attribution) and SPACE_UNIT2 (identity/name only). They answer the same space-unit identity questions but differ in organization linkage and coverage.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_facility_organization_dimension\", \"desc\": \"Organization dimension tables describing the institute's hierarchical organization tree used for facilities/space attribution: FCLT_ORGANIZATION (keyed by FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY, with DLC_KEY/DLC_NAME) and FAC_ORGANIZATION (keyed by ORGANIZATION_KEY, with D_CODE). They answer the same questions about organization names, hierarchy levels, parent/major organizations, assignable flags, and HR cross-references, but belong to different table families and coverage.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_room_major_use_classification\", \"desc\": \"Lookup tables classifying rooms by major use (classrooms, offices, laboratories, residential, circulation, etc.) with a short code, description, and assignable-space flag. They cover the current classification in the FCLT and FAC table families and the fiscal-period historical classification in the FCLT family, jointly answering questions about what a room is primarily used for and whether that use counts as assignable space.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_building_inventory\", \"desc\": \"Tables recording the physical building inventory and its attributes (number/name, type, ownership, site, campus sector, access level, gross/assignable/non-assignable areas, number of rooms, key dates): the current FCLT_* family snapshot, its fiscal-period history (in two date-format variants), the FAC_* family snapshot, and the lightweight space-domain building lookup. They jointly answer questions about building characteristics, areas, and room counts, but differ in time coverage, table family, attribute richness, and area units.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_dept_hr_org_hierarchy\", \"desc\": \"Tables describing the institute's department/lab/center (DLC) and HR organization hierarchies: the HR organization unit dimension in two feed variants (HR_ORG_UNIT, HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW), the master department standard hierarchy path (MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY), its DLC-to-administrative-object link table (MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY_LINKS), and the direct-parent department lookup (MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT). They jointly answer questions about which HR department/area a DLC or organization belongs to, the hierarchy path or parent of a department, and HR department names/codes/levels, and are joined to FCLT_ORGANIZATION via DLC_KEY for facilities/space attribution. They differ in hierarchy representation (full path vs direct parent vs HR unit attributes), unit coverage, and companion columns.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_floor_inventory\", \"desc\": \"Tables recording the floor level of buildings: the current FCLT_* family floor inventory with floor areas, the FAC_* family floor snapshot with the same structure, the fiscal-period historical floor table, and the lightweight space-domain floor lookup. They jointly answer questions about floor numbers and per-floor assignable/non-assignable areas, but differ in time coverage, table family, and attribute richness.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_department_dimension\", \"desc\": \"Lookup tables describing academic departments and their school attribution: the SIS department dimension, the student-facing department lookup, and the SIS administrative department (contact information). They answer questions about department names, full names, school code/name, degree-granting status, budget codes, and department phone numbers, but differ in attribute coverage.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_subject_offering_facts\", \"desc\": \"Fact tables recording subjects offered per term from different business processes: the course catalog (planned catalog attributes), the registrar's section/subject offering records (actual sections and enrollment), subject-level summaries (final enrollment statistics), the textbook information program (subjects tracked for course materials), and library reserve processing (subjects with library reserve activity). They share subject identity (SUBJECT_ID, TERM_CODE) and department attribution but differ in granularity, enrollment semantics, and available measures.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_person_directory\", \"desc\": \"Tables describing people of the institute keyed by MIT_ID: the primary employee directory (contact details, titles, HR department), the Drupal-sourced employee feed (employee group/type, appointment flags, HR org unit), the person master table (payroll rank, position title, active flag), the HR faculty roster (appointment type, terminal degree, emeritus status), the OPA current-person snapshot (HR job/appointment attributes, faculty flag, sabbatical), and the student directory (students with department attribution and student year). They jointly answer questions about who a person is, their contact details, job/appointment attributes, and whether they are employee, faculty, or student; responsible faculty in subject offering tables resolve to these tables via RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_MIT_ID = MIT_ID.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_building_address\", \"desc\": \"Tables recording the postal/street addresses of buildings: the current FCLT_* family address table (multiple purpose-typed address rows per building), its fiscal-period historical counterpart, the FAC_* family address snapshot, and the single-text address fields of the space-domain BUILDINGS lookup. They jointly answer questions about where a building is located (street number/name, city, state, postal code), but differ in time coverage, address decomposition, and table family.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_time_dimension\", \"desc\": \"Time dimension tables of the warehouse at three granularities: TIME_DAY (one row per calendar date, with fiscal/calendar year and period, academic year, financial aid year, day of week, and the academic term code/description of the day), TIME_MONTH (one row per fiscal period in YYYYMM format, covering fiscal years 1996-2035, with fiscal quarter, calendar month, academic term, and financial aid year mappings), and TIME_QUARTER (one row per fiscal quarter, covering fiscal years 2000-2035, with quarter dates, payroll certification deadlines, and quarter status flags). They jointly answer questions about when fiscal periods/quarters/days run, which fiscal/calendar/academic year a date or month belongs to, and how day-level records roll up to months and quarters. They link to each other via FISCAL_PERIOD (day-month), FY_QUARTER_CODE (month-quarter), and FISCAL_YEAR (month-quarter association within the same fiscal year, fanning out months across all quarters of the year), and to the academic term tables via TIME_DAY.ACADEMIC_TERM_CODE or TIME_MONTH.ACADEMIC_TERM = TERM_CODE.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_iap_activities\", \"desc\": \"Tables describing Independent Activities Period (IAP) activities offered in January terms: activity details (title, enrollment type, max enrollment, fee, cancellation flags), sessions (location, date, times), sponsors (name, type), categories, and persons. They jointly answer questions about IAP activity counts, enrollment capacity, fees, session scheduling, and sponsorship.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_course_material_programs\", \"desc\": \"Tables covering course material provisioning: the Textbook Information Program (TIP) tracking textbook adoption status per subject offering, and library reserve processing tracking catalog items placed on reserve for subjects. They jointly answer questions about which subjects have course materials/textbooks, material status (TIP statuses such as 'RQ' Required, 'EO' Electronic options; library statuses such as 'U' Unknown, 'Y' Required Course Material), ISBNs, record counts, and reserve catalog item attributes. The two programs are linked by SUBJECT_ID + TERM_CODE.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_moira_mailing_lists\", \"desc\": \"Tables of the Moira mailing-list/group domain: the list master (one row per list with name, description, active flag, and type flags such as mailing list, group, NFS group, public, hidden), the membership detail (one row per list member with member login, full name, MIT ID, and last update date), and the owner lookup (one row per owner entity with owner name and owner type LIST/USER/KERBEROS). They jointly answer questions about which lists exist and their properties, who belongs to a list, and who owns a list; MOIRA_LIST is the parent of MOIRA_LIST_DETAIL via MOIRA_LIST_KEY, and MOIRA_LIST_OWNER is referenced by MOIRA_LIST_DETAIL via MOIRA_LIST_OWNER_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_academic_term_dimension\", \"desc\": \"Tables describing academic terms and their calendar/status attributes. They jointly answer questions about when terms run, which academic/financial-aid/degree year a term belongs to, and whether a term is current, previous, future, or regular. Coverage differs: the full historical term list, the status-tracked term subset, and the three-row relative term parameter reference.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_course_catalog_sources\", \"desc\": \"Tables providing catalog-level subject attributes (titles, unit structure, grading rules, HGN level, requirement attributes, offering-term flags) from different source systems: the warehouse course catalog, the CIS course catalog feed, and the Drupal course catalog feed. They answer the same catalog-attribute questions but differ in source system, extra columns, and join paths to department/subject-code lookups.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_cip_program_classification\", \"desc\": \"Lookup tables of the Classification of Instructional Programs (CIP) used to classify courses/instructional programs into two-digit categories, four-digit series, and six-digit program codes, with revision version years (1990/2000/2010/2020). CIP holds the current single-version classification (one row per program code, with a change NOTE), while CIP_WITH_VERSION preserves every revision of each program code across versions. Both join to SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION via PROGRAM_CODE = CIP_PROGRAM_CODE to attribute courses to CIP programs and categories.\"}], \"column_concept\": [{\"id\": \"column_concept_num_of_rooms\", \"desc\": \"NUM_OF_ROOMS columns recording how many rooms a building contains, replicated across the current and historical building tables of both families. The building-table columns hold the current room count (one value per building); the history-table columns hold the room count at each fiscal period, used for room-count statistics (average, range, variance, minimum) across a building's history records.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_space_unit_key\", \"desc\": \"Space unit key columns identifying the organizational space-assignment unit across the space dimension and fact tables. SPACE_UNIT_KEY is the join key linking SPACE_DETAIL room rows to space unit identity (name/code) and, through SPACE_UNIT, to the owning facilities organization.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_facility_organization_key\", \"desc\": \"Facility organization key columns attributing space units and rooms to organizations in the hierarchical organization tree. Two naming conventions exist across table families (FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY in FCLT_*/SPACE_* tables vs ORGANIZATION_KEY in FAC_* tables) with the same value domain.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_building_room\", \"desc\": \"Combined building-room identifier columns (e.g. '1-080') appearing in both the space assignment fact table and the facilities room inventory. They identify the same physical room concept but come from different business processes with different coverage and companion measures.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_assignable_area\", \"desc\": \"Assignable-area measure columns at different granularity levels and time semantics: building-level current and per-fiscal-period assignable area, floor-level assignable area, and the space-domain assignable square footage. All FCLT_*/FAC_* columns are in square meters; BUILDINGS.BLDG_ASSIGNABLE_SQUARE_FOOTAGE is in square feet. Choosing the right column determines whether the measure is a building total, a floor total, a historical value, or a space-assignment figure.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_office_location\", \"desc\": \"OFFICE_LOCATION columns recording where a person's office/desk is, replicated across the person-directory tables (SE_PERSON, MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY, EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY, DRUPAL_EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY). All hold a building or building-room text identifier in the same value domain as FCLT_ROOMS.BUILDING_ROOM, but they describe different populations (employee/person master vs student vs primary employee directory vs Drupal employee feed) and differ sharply in non-null coverage and in how many values are building-room ('BLDG-ROOM') versus building-only ('BLDG'). Choosing the right column determines whose office is reported and whether room-level joins to FCLT_ROOMS succeed.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_access_level\", \"desc\": \"Access level columns recorded at three granularity levels of the facilities domain plus the space-planning room feed: building-level ACCESS_LEVEL_CODE/ACCESS_LEVEL_NAME (current and per-fiscal-period history), floor-level ACCESS_LEVEL, and room-level ACCESS_LEVEL (FCLT_ROOMS, FAC_ROOMS, ZPM_ROOMS_LOAD). They share a numeric value domain (observed 0-3) but describe the access restriction of different physical objects or come from different feeds, so filters and joins must target the granularity and table family the question refers to.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_dlc_key\", \"desc\": \"Department/Lab/Center key columns (values like 'D_AEROASTRO', 'D_IDSS', 'D_BIOLOGY') identifying a DLC across the facilities, HR, space, and academic-department domains. They are the universal cross-domain join key linking facilities organizations and space units to HR organization units, the master department hierarchy, and academic departments. Naming and completeness vary: DLC_KEY in most tables, D_CODE in MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT, DLC_CODE in the master hierarchy tables; some columns carry composite values ('D_DSL:HQ') or nulls.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_department_name\", \"desc\": \"Department name columns across subject offering, catalog, lookup, employee, and library reserve instructor tables. Two academic naming conventions exist (DEPARTMENT_NAME vs OFFER_DEPT_NAME) with the same academic value domain; LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR.DEPARTMENT also holds academic departments but in a 'COURSE_NUMBER - Department Name' prefixed format (e.g. '18 - Mathematics'); EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME shares the column name but holds the HR organizational unit name (different value domain). Choosing the right one depends on the table family, the value format, whether the department is the catalog owner or the actual offering department, and whether an academic or HR department is meant.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_enrollment_measures\", \"desc\": \"Enrollment measure columns across subject offering, summary, textbook-program, and library tables. Two families exist: NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS (student headcount snapshots) and SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER (official registrar enrollment), at section, subject, or program scope.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_master_subject_id\", \"desc\": \"Master subject identifier columns (MASTER_SUBJECT_ID and its sortable variant MASTER_SUBJECT_ID_SORT) replicated across the registrar offering tables, the subject summary, the textbook program, the library reserve program, and the CIS course catalog. For clustered subjects (e.g. joint or cross-listed offerings), the master subject identifier points to the leading subject of the cluster, so joining on it matches offerings that share the same master subject even when their own SUBJECT_ID differs. SUBJECT_ID/SUBJECT_ID_SORT identify the subject itself, while MASTER_SUBJECT_ID/MASTER_SUBJECT_ID_SORT identify the cluster's master; the _SORT columns are the sortable forms of the same values used for cross-table joins.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_material_status_key\", \"desc\": \"Material status key columns of the textbook program (TIP) and library reserve program. Both are coded status references decoded by their own lookup tables (key value equals code value), with independent value domains: TIP statuses ('RQ' Required, 'EO' Electronic options, 'RC' Recommended, 'PC' Val-u option, 'BR' Bookstore recommends, 'CL' Go to class first, 'NM' Course has no materials, 'U' Unknown, plus NULL-description keys) vs library reserve statuses ('U' Unknown, 'R' null description, 'N' Non-Required Course Material, 'O' Reserve only, 'X' No Required Textbook, 'Y' Required Course Material).\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_term_code\", \"desc\": \"Term code columns in YYYYTT format (e.g. '2025FA', '2019SP', '2021JA', '2012SU'; TT = FA Fall, SP Spring, JA January/IAP, SU Summer) appearing across term dimension and fact tables. They are the universal join key linking subject offerings, textbook materials, library reserves, and IAP activities to term attributes.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_subject_id\", \"desc\": \"Subject identifier columns shared across catalog, registrar, textbook-program, and library tables. SUBJECT_ID is the cross-domain subject join key in 'CODE.NUMBER' format (e.g. '18.01'); it appears in every subject-related fact table but at different grains and program scopes.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_fiscal_period\", \"desc\": \"Fiscal period code columns in YYYYMM format (e.g. '199602' = FY1996 period 2, '201505') appearing in two distinct roles: as the primary key of the month-grain time dimension (TIME_MONTH.FISCAL_PERIOD, also mirrored in TIME_DAY.FISCAL_PERIOD for day-to-month linkage), and as the snapshot-period stamp of the facilities historical tables (FCLT_BUILDING_HIST, FCLT_BUILDING_HIST_1, FCLT_BUILDING_ADDRESS_HIST, FCLT_FLOOR_HIST, FCLT_ROOMS_HIST, FCLT_MAJOR_USE_HIST). Both roles share the same YYYYMM value domain, but the time dimension uses it for calendar grouping while the history tables use it to mark when a facilities snapshot was taken.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_building_type_site\", \"desc\": \"Building classification columns replicated across the current and historical building tables of both table families: BUILDING_TYPE ('ACADEMIC', 'SERVICE', 'RESIDENT') and SITE ('MIT', 'BATES', 'LINC', 'BOS', etc.). They carry the same value domain but differ in time semantics: the building-table columns are the current classification, while the history-table columns are the classification recorded at each fiscal period, so filtering by one versus the other can select different building sets.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_total_units\", \"desc\": \"Total credit unit columns replicated across catalog and registrar subject tables. They represent the same business quantity (total credit units of a subject) but come from different processes and pair with different companion unit columns.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_year_columns\", \"desc\": \"Year columns across term, catalog, and time dimension tables representing different year systems: academic year, fiscal year, financial aid year, and degree year. Selecting the correct year system is essential for yearly grouping and partitioning.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_hass_attribute\", \"desc\": \"HASS (Humanities, Arts, and Social Sciences) attribute code and description columns. The code columns appear in the three course catalog feeds and in the CIS_HASS_ATTRIBUTE lookup; description columns exist in three variants: the catalog-embedded HASS_ATTRIBUTE_DESC, the lookup's DESCRIPTION_ON_FORM (registration-form wording), and DESCRIPTION_IN_BULLETIN (short bulletin wording). Selecting the right description variant depends on the wording requested by the question.\"}]}}"
    },
    {
      "role": "tool",
      "tool_call_id": "call_0f736c5f79244dfba5702f48",
      "name": "semantic_search",
      "content": "{\"ok\": true, \"count\": 20, \"items_by_type\": {\"table\": [{\"id\": \"FCLT_ROOMS\", \"desc\": \"Facilities room inventory table: one row per physical room with building/floor keys, room identifiers, use classifications (major/minor use), organization assignment, area in square meters, access level, and geographic coordinates. Joins to FCLT_BUILDING via FCLT_BUILDING_KEY; referenced by COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.MEET_PLACE via FCLT_ROOM_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"FAC_ROOMS\", \"desc\": \"Facilities room snapshot table with the same room inventory structure as FCLT_ROOMS (building/floor keys, room identifiers, major/minor use classifications, organization assignment, area, access level, coordinates) but keyed by FAC_ROOM_KEY and joining the FAC_* family (FAC_BUILDING, FAC_FLOOR, FAC_ORGANIZATION). Used as an alternative room source when FAC_* family keys are involved.\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_ORGANIZATION\", \"desc\": \"Facilities organization dimension table: one row per organization in the institute's hierarchical organization tree (levels 1-6, from institute-wide down to sub-units), with organization identifiers and names, parent and major-organization attribution, hierarchy level, assignable-space flag, course number for academic departments, description, DLC (department/lab/center) key and name, and cross-references to HR organization units. Parent of SPACE_UNIT (space assigned to organizations) and referenced by FCLT_ROOMS via FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY for room occupancy attribution.\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_FLOOR\", \"desc\": \"Facilities floor inventory table: one row per floor of a building (floor key formatted '<building key>-<floor>'), with floor number/label, gross, assignable and non-assignable areas of the floor, sort sequence, level identifier, building wing, and access level. Child of FCLT_BUILDING via FCLT_BUILDING_KEY and parent of FCLT_ROOMS via FCLT_FLOOR_KEY; used for per-floor area aggregation and floor-level filtering (e.g. floors with assignable area above a threshold).\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_MAJOR_USE\", \"desc\": \"Facilities major use classification lookup table (FCLT family): one row per major use code (e.g. CLASSRMS classrooms, OFFICES offices, LABS laboratories, RESIDENT residential) with its short code, description, and assignable-space flag. Joined from FCLT_ROOMS via FCLT_MAJOR_USE_KEY to decode a room's major use; current snapshot only, use FCLT_MAJOR_USE_HIST for fiscal-period historical variants.\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_ROOMS_HIST\", \"desc\": \"Historical facilities room table: one row per room per fiscal period (FISCAL_PERIOD in YYYYMM format; current data covers period 201505), preserving each room's identifiers, floor, use classifications, organization assignment, area, access level, and coordinates over time. Fiscal-period counterpart of FCLT_ROOMS; joins to current room records via FCLT_ROOM_KEY and to buildings via FCLT_BUILDING_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"SPACE_UNIT\", \"desc\": \"Space unit dimension table: one row per space unit (an organizational space-assignment unit such as a department, program, or office that receives space allocation), with space unit key/code, space unit name, the facilities organization it belongs to, and DLC key. Bridges FCLT_ORGANIZATION (organization attribution) and SPACE_DETAIL (rooms assigned to the space unit); used to group room counts and space statistics by space unit.\"}, {\"id\": \"FAC_FLOOR\", \"desc\": \"Facilities floor snapshot table (FAC_* family): one row per floor of a building with floor number/label, gross, assignable and non-assignable areas, sort sequence, level, wing, and access level. Same floor structure as FCLT_FLOOR but keyed by FLOOR_KEY/BUILDING_KEY joining FAC_ROOMS.FLOOR_KEY and FAC_BUILDING.FAC_BUILDING_KEY; used as the floor source when FAC_* family keys are involved.\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_BUILDING\", \"desc\": \"Facilities building inventory table: one row per physical building with building number/name, type (e.g. ACADEMIC), ownership, use, occupancy class, gross/assignable/non-assignable areas, number of rooms, key dates (built/acquired/occupied), site and geographic coordinates. Parent of FCLT_ROOMS via FCLT_BUILDING_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"FAC_BUILDING\", \"desc\": \"Facilities building snapshot table (FAC_* family): one row per physical building with the same building attribute structure as FCLT_BUILDING (number/name, type, ownership, use, occupancy class, gross/assignable/non-assignable areas, number of rooms, key dates, site, coordinates) but keyed by FAC_BUILDING_KEY and joining the FAC_* family (FAC_ROOMS, FAC_FLOOR, FAC_BUILDING_ADDRESS, FAC_ORGANIZATION). Used as the building dimension when FAC_* family keys are involved; FCLT_BUILDING is the counterpart in the FCLT_* family.\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY\", \"desc\": \"Bridge table mapping facilities organizations to their department/lab/center (DLC) keys: one row per organization-DLC key assignment. Used to filter organizations that have a non-null DLC key assignment before joining FCLT_ORGANIZATION (via FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY or DLC_KEY) for DLC-level facility and room statistics.\"}, {\"id\": \"FAC_ORGANIZATION\", \"desc\": \"Facilities organization snapshot table with the same hierarchical organization structure as FCLT_ORGANIZATION (organization identifiers, parent/major organization, level, assignable flag, course number, description, HR cross-references) but keyed by ORGANIZATION_KEY and carrying D_CODE instead of DLC_KEY/DLC_NAME. Contains fewer organizations than FCLT_ORGANIZATION; used as an alternative organization dimension in FAC_* family queries.\"}, {\"id\": \"SPACE_DETAIL\", \"desc\": \"Space assignment detail fact table: one row per physical room assigned to a space unit, with building/floor/space-unit/space-usage keys, room identifiers (building-room number and name, room number), room square footage, room counter, and building component. Used to count rooms per space unit or per building, and to analyze room size and usage distribution. Joins to SPACE_UNIT via SPACE_UNIT_KEY, FCLT_BUILDING via BUILDING_KEY, SPACE_FLOOR via FLOOR_KEY, and SPACE_USAGE via SPACE_USAGE_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_FLOOR_HIST\", \"desc\": \"Historical facilities floor table: one row per floor per fiscal period (FISCAL_PERIOD in YYYYMM format, covering 201505-201602), preserving each floor's number/label, gross, assignable and non-assignable areas, sort sequence, level, wing, and access level over time. Fiscal-period counterpart of FCLT_FLOOR; joins to buildings via FCLT_BUILDING_KEY and to current floor records via FCLT_FLOOR_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"SPACE_FLOOR\", \"desc\": \"Space-domain floor lookup table: one row per floor key with the floor number/label and floor name. Referenced by SPACE_DETAIL via FLOOR_KEY to attach floor identity to assigned rooms; a lightweight floor reference without the area measures carried by FCLT_FLOOR or FAC_FLOOR.\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_ORGANIZATION_HIST\", \"desc\": \"22 columns in total\"}, {\"id\": \"FAC_MAJOR_USE\", \"desc\": \"Facilities major use classification lookup table (FAC family): same major use code/description/assignable structure as FCLT_MAJOR_USE but keyed by MAJOR_USE_KEY and joining the FAC_* family (FAC_ROOMS.MAJOR_USE_KEY). Used as the major use decoder when FAC_ROOMS is the room source.\"}, {\"id\": \"ZPM_ROOMS_LOAD\", \"desc\": \"Space-planning room load table: one row per room record from the space planning feed, with the building-room identifier, building component, floor (numeric or label such as 'G9'), space usage text (e.g. 'DSGN STUDIO', 'CONF RM'), space unit code, HR organization unit id, and room access level. Links rooms to SPACE_UNIT via SPACE_UNIT_CODE and to FCLT_ORGANIZATION/HR_ORG_UNIT via HR_ORG_UNIT_ID; used for floor/access-level/space-usage room analysis from the space-planning perspective, without the area and use-key columns carried by FCLT_ROOMS.\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_BUILDING_HIST\", \"desc\": \"Historical facilities building snapshot table: one row per building per fiscal period (FISCAL_PERIOD in YYYYMM format, covering 201505-201906, 48 periods, ~255 buildings), preserving each building's attributes over time: identifiers and names, gross/assignable/non-assignable areas, site, campus sector, access level, building type, ownership type, use, occupancy class, height, cost center/collector references, coordinates, and number of rooms. Used for fiscal-period building history analysis (area/room-count trends, dispersion statistics across historical records); use FCLT_BUILDING for the current snapshot. Date columns (DATE_BUILT/DATE_ACQUIRED/DATE_OCCUPIED) are stored in MM/DD/YYYY format; FCLT_BUILDING_HIST_1 is the variant storing them in DD-MON-YY format.\"}, {\"id\": \"BUILDINGS\", \"desc\": \"Space-domain building lookup table: one row per building with building key/number, building name, street and mailing addresses as single text fields, gross and assignable square footage (in square feet), and a building counter. Referenced by SPACE_DETAIL via BUILDING_KEY; a lightweight building reference for space-assignment reporting, without the type/ownership/site classification carried by FCLT_BUILDING or FAC_BUILDING.\"}]}}"
